WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.610
Chemists picture a gas as
tiny particles in constant,

2
00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:07.710
random motion, colliding with
the walls of their container.

3
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:11.810
Test that model on helium,
and it works almost perfectly.

4
00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:15.770
Test it on ammonia, and the
predictions start to drift.

5
00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:18.050
Same model, two gases.

6
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:23.730
Why does helium behave almost exactly as
the model predicts, but ammonia doesn't?

7
00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:27.630
In this mission, you'll list the
assumptions behind the ideal gas model,

8
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:32.030
and find the conditions where
real gases stray furthest from it.

9
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:36.550
You'll read a graph that shows how
far a real gas strays from ideal.

10
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:41.330
Your mission: explain why some gases
behave less ideally than others.
